  "body": "MAINLINE-044 complete. No qualified installed-hull fatigue life. Original mooring-pad core shear exceeds minimum strength (SF 0.7143); the corrected metal plates alone reach the declared fatigue-design index in about 950 days. Daily thermal-only core projections are 3,697 days under 037 versus 18,816 days under 037b’s 200 F free-edge fix. These transfer denser-core fatigue data and assumed mean-stress rules. The small 037b fix leaves the pads unchanged and does not cover all combined scarf loads. Actual-geometry vacuum top-ups span 27.56 Pa initially and 8.34 Pa late-year; full venting is a separate pressure cycle. Gross-area adhesive shear cannot qualify sparse wall-foot/fillet contact. A strict ten-year pad allocation plus 60:1 scarf adds 36.66 kg, exceeding the unchanged floating budget; Be-sheet, scarf, bond, local buckling and environment qualifications remain open. No ten-year whole-hull claim. The filed calculation, source data, cycle ledger, mass options and NFI register include 037b. Twenty-one numerical checks, five physical/allocation assertions and 75 input/source pins pass; all 132 manifest entries verify. Nineteen new NFI plus thirteen inherited 037b items remain nonblocking. The brief names no successor; stopping after this report.",
